  "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=\\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & y=-\\frac{5}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{5}{3})=\\frac{10}{3}\\,\u21d2\\,x=\\frac{10}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
